**ai-teammate** (2026-10-06):

⚠️ **IMPORTANT: single-shot double-Esc abort — documented CI race (adopt the sibling's 3-attempt loop)**

This PTY test has never executed (PTY allocation blocked locally — the PR says CI's PTY leg is the real gate), and its abort sequence is the exact write shape the sibling suite had to harden:

`test/integration/fa_cli_thinking_abort_test.dart` (same rig, same mock) says:

```dart
// ONE write carrying both presses — the exact wire shape of a fast
// double-tap that the decoder used to swallow whole. Re-sent up to
// twice on a ~3s probe: on a loaded CI runner a single-shot write
// raced the 10ms lone-escape timer window (run 36732676599)
// and the run streamed on untouched.
var aborted = harness.screenText.contains('abort');
for (var attempt = 0; attempt < 3 && !aborted; attempt++) {
  if (attempt > 0) harness.sendText('\x1b\x1b');
  ...
}
```

Here the `sendText('\x1b\x1b')` at line 68 fires once and the test then waits 10s for the busy row to clear — on a loaded runner the swallowed-write race documented in run 36732676599 turns this into a red PTY shard (flaky, load-dependent), and each wasted round costs the 15–20 min rework loop.

Suggested fix — reuse the sibling's pattern:

```dart
harness.sendText('\x1b\x1b');
var aborted = !harness.screenText.contains('Working');
for (var attempt = 0; attempt < 3 && !aborted; attempt++) {
  if (attempt > 0) harness.sendText('\x1b\x1b');
  final deadline = DateTime.now().add(const Duration(seconds: 5));
  while (DateTime.now().isBefore(deadline)) {
    if (!harness.screenText.contains('Working')) break;
    await Future<void>.delayed(const Duration(milliseconds: 100));
  }
  aborted = !harness.screenText.contains('Working');
}
expect(aborted, isTrue, reason: 'the run kept streaming after Esc Esc');
```

The liveness assertions (lines 41–60) are unaffected and well-formed.

